LM Training

1. Overview
This document describes the Language Model (LM) training process, including the Transformer architecture, training method, and positional encoding details.

2. Transformer Architecture
- Model: TransformerLM
- Embedding: Input embedding layer (torch.nn.Embedding)
- Encoder: Stack of TransformerEncoderLayers (default: 12 layers, configurable)
- Attention: Multi-head self-attention (nhead=8 by default)
- Feedforward: Two-layer feedforward network (dim_feedforward=2048)
- Output: Linear layer mapping to vocabulary size
- Weight tying: Optionally ties input embedding and output linear weights
- Dropout: 0.1 (configurable)

3. Teacher Forcing Training
- Training uses teacher forcing: During training, the model receives the ground-truth previous token as input for predicting the next token.
- In train.py, compute_loss() passes x (input tokens) and y (target tokens, shifted by one position) to the model, which is standard teacher forcing for LM training.

4. Positional Encoding
- Type: Relative positional encoding (RelPositionalEncoding)
- Implementation: Sine and cosine functions of different frequencies
- Maximum length: Default is 5000 positions; if JIT tracing is enabled, up to 10,000 positions
- The positional encoding is dynamically extended as needed for input length

